Read ALL four v8 verdicts, the FULL v9 design and its diff from v8, the oracle README and evidence, the oracle source/test, and check claims against actual Java and current Go. v9 answers v8: the peel's empirical cap is replaced by a geometric removal floor (after round r at least 2^(r+1)-1 members have left M, shortfall taken from members farthest from the other child's centroid) with a structural bound of floor(log2(n-1)) refits, measured on tight high-dimensional cores where the v8 peel ran one round per outlier, plus a transaction-time budget that ends the peel at the reconcile before FDB's 5 s limit; the target's second throw site KMeans.java:136 is named and the n<k rule labelled as Go's; the reconcile failure is a distinct Go-only ClusterUnsplittableError with a per-retry-owner classification, reachable in deferred mode too, and its relief threshold difference (hard max vs max) declared; task poisoning is decided once in the execution wrapper for ANY error returned after the removal is buffered (cancellation included); consumerOutcome takes isolation as a parameter (serializable in runTask, snapshot only for the skip), includes the phase-1 re-enqueue exit, returns the bounce's list and pick for runTask to consume, states exactly what it does not predict (bounce follow-up quantizer, reconcile failure, conservative n<k skip) and names one fixture per arm; the claim-race wait cap is injectable; the population reconciliation and a frozen-tree just test are recorded (item 19), and 119 skipped conformance specs inherited from master are tracked in TODO.md. Challenge sufficiency and interactions with the rest of the design, not only whether the requested words appear. Distinguish measured target facts from remaining source hypotheses.
Preserved boundaries: GuardiANN executes in merger-supplied transactions (no invented child runner); SPFresh independent algorithms/LIRE; approved raw/nullable-array/scalar/sort extensions; C++ 7.3.77; format max 15/default 14; Lucene is separate upgrade-wide work, not Go TEXT; WS-D cannot complete with a refusal or fake backend.
